# Paws & Claws: Adding a New Feature with OpenHands
# This demo shows an AI agent adding Pet Grooming Services to an existing pet store.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - demorec installed (pip install demorec)
#   - The petstore-frontend repo checked out with both branches available
#   - npm dependencies installed
#
# Run: demorec record demo/frontend-feature-demo.demorec

Output demo/frontend-feature-demo.mp4
Set Width 1280
Set Height 720

# @voice edge:jenny

# ─────────────────────────────────────
# ACT 1: Show the existing pet store
# ─────────────────────────────────────

@mode terminal
Set Theme "Dracula"

# @narrate:before "Let's start with our existing Paws and Claws pet store website."

Type "cd petstore-frontend && git checkout main"
Enter
Sleep 1s

Type "npm run dev -- --port 3000 &"
Enter
Sleep 3s

@mode browser

# @narrate:before "Here's our pet store. It has categories for dogs, cats, birds, and fish."

Navigate "http://localhost:3000"
Sleep 3s

Scroll "down" "400"
Sleep 2s

# @narrate:after "Customers can browse pets, filter by category, and add them to their cart."

Scroll "down" "400"
Sleep 2s

# ─────────────────────────────────────
# ACT 2: The feature request
# ─────────────────────────────────────

@mode terminal

# @narrate:before "Now, the business wants to add a new service: pet grooming. Let's ask OpenHands to build this feature."

Type "# Business request: Add a Pet Grooming Services section"
Enter
Sleep 1s
Type "# with service cards, filtering by pet type, and Book Now buttons"
Enter
Sleep 2s

# ─────────────────────────────────────
# ACT 3: Show the feature branch diff
# ─────────────────────────────────────

# @narrate:before "OpenHands created a feature branch with all the changes. Let's look at what was built."

Type "git checkout feature/add-grooming-services"
Enter
Sleep 1s

Type "git diff --stat main"
Enter
Sleep 2s

# @narrate:after "Five files changed: new grooming component, data, styles, and updates to the header and app."

Sleep 2s

# ─────────────────────────────────────
# ACT 4: Preview the new feature
# ─────────────────────────────────────

@mode browser

# @narrate:before "Let's see the result in the browser."

Navigate "http://localhost:3000"
Sleep 2s

# @narrate:before "Notice the new purple Grooming button in the navigation."

Highlight "button.grooming-nav"
Sleep 2s
Unhighlight "button.grooming-nav"

Click "button.grooming-nav"
Sleep 2s

# @narrate:after "A complete grooming services section with six service packages, pricing, and Book Now buttons."

Sleep 2s

Scroll "down" "200"
Sleep 2s

# @narrate:after "The most popular services are highlighted, and you can filter by pet type."

Sleep 3s

# ─────────────────────────────────────
# ACT 5: Code review
# ─────────────────────────────────────

@mode terminal

# @narrate:before "Finally, OpenHands reviews its own code, catching accessibility issues and suggesting design system improvements."

Type "git diff main -- src/components/GroomingServices.jsx | head -40"
Enter
Sleep 3s

# @narrate:after "Clean, well-structured components following the existing patterns. The code review flagged the alert dialog as a UX anti-pattern and suggested promoting hardcoded colors to CSS variables."

Sleep 3s

# @narrate:after "That's how OpenHands helps frontend developers: take an existing codebase, add a polished new feature, preview it in the browser, and review the code. All from a single conversation."

Sleep 2s
